<p>One pattern in the table deserves attention. For <i>Feeling of guilt</i>, {{ g_no.anxious | f1 }}% of the women who answered <i>No</i> report feeling anxious, against {{ g_maybe.anxious | f1 }}% for <i>Maybe</i> and only {{ g_yes.anxious | f1 }}% for <i>Yes</i> (Figure 4.1). The relationship is strong, which is why this question dominates every importance ranking later in the book, but its direction is the opposite of what clinical experience would suggest. It must be read as a property of this dataset, not as evidence about guilt and anxiety in general.</p>
