{{ h2('5.4') }}
<p>Figure 5.2 shows the architecture of the proposed model. The four base models were chosen for diversity: two boosting models with different tree-growing strategies, one bagging model and one neural network. LightGBM is left out of the stack because it is the closest relative of XGBoost and would add little diversity. The meta-learner is deliberately simple. A logistic regression on four probabilities has five parameters, so it cannot overfit the way a deep meta-learner could, and its weights can be read directly.</p>
<figure>
