<section class="chapter" id="appD"><header><div class="label">Appendix D</div><h1>Glossary and Abbreviations</h1><p class="lead">Terms used in this book, in plain language.</p></header>
<div class="tbl long">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th style="width:44mm">Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Answer pattern</td><td>One complete combination of answers to the nine feature questions</td></tr>
      <tr><td>AUC / ROC-AUC</td><td>Area under the receiver operating characteristic curve; 1.0 is perfect ranking, 0.5 is chance</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bagging</td><td>Training many models on resampled data and averaging them</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Balanced accuracy</td><td>Mean of recall and specificity</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Base model</td><td>A model whose predictions feed the meta-learner in a stack</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Boosting</td><td>Building models in sequence, each correcting the errors of the previous ones</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bootstrap</td><td>Resampling the data with replacement to estimate the uncertainty of a statistic</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Brier score</td><td>Mean squared error of predicted probabilities; lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Calibration</td><td>Agreement between predicted probabilities and observed frequencies</td></tr>
      <tr><td>CI</td><td>Confidence interval</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Conformal prediction</td><td>A method that returns a set of answers with a guaranteed coverage rate</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Counterfactual</td><td>The smallest change to the inputs that would change the prediction</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Coverage</td><td>Share of cases in which a prediction set contains the true answer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cramér's V</td><td>Strength of association between two categorical variables, from 0 to 1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>CV</td><td>Cross-validation: repeated training and testing on different parts of the data</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Data leakage</td><td>Information from test data reaching the model during training</td></tr>
      <tr><td>EPDS</td><td>Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale, a validated screening questionnaire</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Faithfulness</td><td>How well an explanation reflects what the model actually does</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Friedman test</td><td>Non-parametric test for differences among several models measured on the same folds</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GAD-7</td><td>Generalised Anxiety Disorder 7-item scale</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Grouped CV</td><td>Cross-validation in which all rows of a group stay in the same fold</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Holm correction</td><td>Adjustment of p-values when several tests are made</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hybrid Stack</td><td>The proposed model: CatBoost, XGBoost, random forest and MLP combined by logistic regression</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LIME</td><td>Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations</td></tr>
      <tr><td>MCC</td><td>Matthews correlation coefficient</td></tr>
      <tr><td>McNemar test</td><td>Test comparing two models on the cases where they disagree</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Meta-learner</td><td>The model that combines the base models' predictions in a stack</td></tr>
      <tr><td>MLP</td><td>Multilayer perceptron, a feed-forward neural network</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One-hot encoding</td><td>Representing each possible answer as its own 0/1 column</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Out-of-fold prediction</td><td>A prediction for a person made by a model that was not trained on that person</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Permutation importance</td><td>Loss of accuracy when one feature is shuffled</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Recall (sensitivity)</td><td>Share of true positives that the model finds</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SHAP</td><td>SHapley Additive exPlanations</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Specificity</td><td>Share of true negatives that the model correctly clears</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stacking</td><td>Combining several models by training another model on their predictions</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stratified split</td><td>A split that keeps the class proportions equal in every part</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Twin</td><td>A test person whose exact answer pattern also occurs in the training set</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wilcoxon signed-rank test</td><td>Non-parametric paired test for two models measured on the same folds</td></tr>
      <tr><td>XAI</td><td>Explainable artificial intelligence</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
</section>

